  ],
  "detail": "Native full-history and reduced-owner continuations now own a scope inside their existing verified-record callback, capturing only newly appended receipts. Publisher and epoch classification share that exact owned syntax with saved verification. Complete only after old coverage, current, received-prefix and actual ownership checks; finally always disposes. Changed retained bytes still refuse before capture; own-publisher/history/unknown-observation fallback stays. Reduced-owner cold indexing now supplies its actual memo byte observation, retaining the same graph/clone/logical ceilings. Independent normalized AST review preserves every existing operation, cleanup and guard; exact retained-prefix comparison and its independent full oracle are unchanged.",
  "validation": "Four new controls; before one duplicate-parse failure and three passes, after all pass. Interior extent continuation/full agreement, later legacy record scope, predecessor immutability, changed-row early fallback, own publisher and physical witness failure covered. Initial new test annotation was too narrow for an optional index; corrected only that new annotation and retained failure. Types,205focused cases in25files,18unchanged legacy and full323files/3161cases/one existing skip pass124.19s (command125.001s) at approved240s; other deadlines unchanged. Quality, format,17registry checks, inventory and10controls pass. Three runtime hashes and nine source-site line moves reviewed; all old tests, constructions and obligations retained.",
  "summary": "New-only scopes now cover native and reduced-owner continuations. Four controls pass;205focused/18legacy plus full323files/3161cases/one skip pass124.19s. Existing operations/guards remain AST-exact after explicit normalization.",
  "limitations": "No physical browser cold, image, activation, timing or RAM credit. Live owned parsing/dense writer, dual audit, G8/B, floor lifecycle, old artifacts/cold/rollback and Stage5/6 remain. No trust/format/wire/default/limit/gate/deadline change, commit or deployment.",
  "decisionTitle": "Scope continuation syntax after exact retained-prefix comparison",
  "decision": "A continuation captures only its new physical rows, never its retained predecessor. A failed bound, witness, coverage or lifecycle check abandons the whole scope and existing fallback remains. Actual proof-byte observation is required to index a reduced binary suffix.",
  "next": "Harden live original syntax and encoding as one owned call, then dense native writing, dual audit, G8/B and floor/lifecycle/old artifacts/cold/rollback. Continue automatically after each frozen phase under the existing decision boundaries.",
